<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Štip</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Astibos, Astibo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Štip is a city in the eastern part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-macedonia">North Macedonia</a>, on the Bregalnica River. In antiquity, as Astibos, it was one of the centres of the kingdom of Paeonia, and it later lay on the Roman road through the region. It was held in turn by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bulgaria">Bulgaria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbia">Serbia</a> before passing to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottomans</a> in the late 14th century, and is now a regional centre of the textile industry.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/stip.jpg" alt="Štip" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: This illustration was made by Rašo. An email to Rašo would be appreciated too. · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%C5%A0tip_23.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
